From: REG-Linux
Subject: [PATCH] device-manager: don't add fbdev when DRM already drives the display

create_devices_from_udev() runs on the device timeout and enumerates the
frame buffer subsystem unconditionally, even when the initial scan already
brought up a DRM renderer for the same output.

ply_device_manager_watch_devices() deliberately scans SUBSYSTEM_INPUT and
SUBSYSTEM_DRM only, so the timeout path is the only place fbdev is added. On
a machine whose DRM driver also exposes fbdev emulation, that re-adds the
very same CRTC a second time and plymouth ends up with two pixel displays:

    adding 1920x1080 pixel display     <- drm,   /dev/dri/card1
    adding 3840x2160 pixel display     <- fbdev, /dev/fb0

The splash is then painted once per display. This normally goes unnoticed
because both renderers agree on the geometry and the two copies land on top
of each other.

On Amlogic they do not agree. meson's fbdev node keeps the mode U-Boot left
behind -- the ODROID-C5 bootloader sets fb_width=3840 / display_width=3840
for its own logo -- so /dev/fb0 reports 3840x2160 with rowstride 15360 while
the connector is running at 1920x1080. The splash is drawn once centred for
a 1920-wide surface and once centred for a 3840-wide one, producing two side
by side copies aligned to the top of the screen. It is invisible on a 4K
panel, where the two geometries happen to coincide.

Guard the fallback on found_drm_device, which is already maintained for
exactly this kind of decision and is consulted three lines further down.

Signed-off-by: REG-Linux <contact@reglinux.org>
diff --git a/src/libply-splash-core/ply-device-manager.c b/src/libply-splash-core/ply-device-manager.c
index 016ac332..4a6437cd 100644
--- a/src/libply-splash-core/ply-device-manager.c
+++ b/src/libply-splash-core/ply-device-manager.c
@@ -1252,7 +1252,22 @@ create_devices_from_udev (ply_device_manager_t *manager)
 
         create_devices_for_subsystem (manager, SUBSYSTEM_INPUT);
         create_devices_for_subsystem (manager, SUBSYSTEM_DRM);
-        create_devices_for_subsystem (manager, SUBSYSTEM_FRAME_BUFFER);
+
+        /* Only fall back to fbdev when nothing is already driving the display
+         * through DRM. The initial scan in ply_device_manager_watch_devices()
+         * deliberately looks at DRM alone; enumerating the frame buffer here
+         * unconditionally re-adds the very same CRTC a second time, through
+         * its fbdev emulation, and plymouth then paints the splash once per
+         * display.
+         *
+         * That stays invisible only while both agree on the geometry. On
+         * Amlogic the fbdev node keeps the mode U-Boot left behind (3840x2160
+         * on the ODROID-C5), so with the panel at 1920x1080 the splash is
+         * drawn once centred for DRM and once centred for a 3840-wide surface,
+         * giving two side by side copies aligned to the top of the screen.
+         */
+        if (!manager->found_drm_device)
+                create_devices_for_subsystem (manager, SUBSYSTEM_FRAME_BUFFER);
 
         if (manager->found_drm_device || manager->found_fb_device)
                 return;
